WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:06.017
Aladdin opened the door, and the magician stepped into the house.

2
00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:07.118
"Aladdin, son of my brother!"

3
00:00:07.198 --> 00:00:07.958
said Magrib.

4
00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:10.119
He placed a basket of figs into Zeba's arms, bowed low, and said, "Wife of my brother!

5
00:00:32.584 --> 00:00:33.544
A small gift."

6
00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:38.366
Then he looked around the room.

7
00:00:38.386 --> 00:00:43.068
"Tell me," he said, "where did your husband once sit?"

8
00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:46.450
Zeba pointed to a cushion by the wall.

9
00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.751
"Oh, my poor brother!"

10
00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:54.913
Magrib cried out—and collapsed into a heap on the cushion.

11
00:00:54.933 --> 00:01:01.856
"This looks like true sadness," whispered Zeba, and she rushed to her guest.

12
00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:06.270
"There's no need to be so distressed," she said.

13
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.211
"Come, let's eat!"

14
00:01:09.391 --> 00:01:13.414
Aladdin helped the magician stand up, and his mother carried in the food.

15
00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:19.597
Then, while they sat and ate, she began to question Magrib.

16
00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:24.220
"Sir, why have I never heard of you before this day?"

17
00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.202
"It is no surprise to me," answered Magrib.

18
00:01:28.222 --> 00:01:32.124
"I left this town, my birthplace, forty years ago."

19
00:01:33.684 --> 00:01:35.225
"My husband was still a boy!"

20
00:01:35.846 --> 00:01:36.547
said Zeba.

21
00:01:37.928 --> 00:01:38.828
Magrib nodded.

22
00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:42.551
"I wandered through many lands," he continued.

23
00:01:42.571 --> 00:01:45.454
"At last, I found my way to Egypt."

24
00:01:45.474 --> 00:01:48.897
"I've heard it is a wonderful place!"

25
00:01:49.557 --> 00:01:50.218
said Aladdin.

26
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:53.080
"Yes, my boy, it is.

27
00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.664
But over time, I became old and homesick for my own country.

28
00:01:58.865 --> 00:02:02.588
I wanted to see my younger brother one more time before my death.

29
00:02:03.932 --> 00:02:05.593
So I journeyed home to find him.

30
00:02:06.113 --> 00:02:07.833
But I'm too late!"

31
00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:10.114
Magrib began to sob.

32
00:02:14.275 --> 00:02:17.036
cannot escape the will of God," said Zeba.

33
00:02:18.236 --> 00:02:20.177
"Here, poor man, eat a bit more!

34
00:02:20.577 --> 00:02:21.837
It will make you feel better."

35
00:02:22.898 --> 00:02:25.558
Magrib took another serving from a big dish.

36
00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.739
"I am comforted," he said.

37
00:02:28.759 --> 00:02:34.425
"Even though my brother has gone, he still lives on in this boy, Aladdin."

38
00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:38.786
Magrib put his hand on Aladdin's shoulder.

39
00:02:38.806 --> 00:02:43.167
"Nephew, you are the head of this house," he said.

40
00:02:43.187 --> 00:02:45.448
"What work have you learned to do?

41
00:02:46.028 --> 00:02:47.788
How do you take care of your good mother?"

42
00:02:49.109 --> 00:02:51.889
Feeling guilty, Aladdin looked at his mother.

43
00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:56.711
"He has learned nothing," the widow said angrily.

44
00:02:56.731 --> 00:02:58.711
"Nothing at all.

45
00:02:59.171 --> 00:03:01.172
All day, he plays games in the streets.

46
00:03:02.752 --> 00:03:06.213
His father died of sadness because this boy would not work."

47
00:03:07.733 --> 00:03:09.394
Then she burst into tears.

48
00:03:09.414 --> 00:03:17.356
"I am the one who works all day and night to take care of this lazy boy!"

49
00:03:19.717 --> 00:03:24.778
Aladdin hung his head in shame, while the magician smiled and comforted the widow.

50
00:03:24.798 --> 00:03:28.619
"Your troubles are over," he said.

51
00:03:28.639 --> 00:03:32.080
"God has blessed me with wealth so that I may help you."

52
00:03:33.852 --> 00:03:37.575
Aladdin looked up brightly, and his mother wiped away her tears.

53
00:03:37.595 --> 00:03:43.100
"My nephew, you must learn a business," said Magrib.

54
00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.163
"It is a disgrace to play all day while your old mother toils."

55
00:03:48.724 --> 00:03:51.567
"You are right, my uncle," Aladdin said quietly.

56
00:03:51.587 --> 00:03:57.371
"Now, boy, don't worry," said Magrib, patting Aladdin on the shoulder.

57
00:03:57.391 --> 00:04:01.014
"I will buy you a shop and fill it with goods.

58
00:04:01.595 --> 00:04:05.401
Then you can be a merchant—buying, selling, and growing rich!"

59
00:04:05.421 --> 00:04:07.903
"A merchant?"

60
00:04:08.283 --> 00:04:08.964
said Aladdin.

61
00:04:08.984 --> 00:04:11.065
"Growing rich?"

62
00:04:11.646 --> 00:04:12.446
added his mother.

63
00:04:17.029 --> 00:04:23.233
She clapped her hands, embraced her son, and whispered into his ear, "This man must truly be your

64
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:28.457
uncle!" "I have eaten enough, and it is now late," said Magrib.

65
00:04:28.477 --> 00:04:32.400
"But I will return in the morning, and we will go to the bazaar.

66
00:04:33.781 --> 00:04:37.254
I will buy Aladdin everything he needs to be a young merchant!"
